Subject: [PATCH] gen3_lite_2f: prefix the ros2_control hardware name

ros2_ws/src/ros2_kortex/ is recorded in this repo's index as a gitlink
(mode 160000) but there is no .gitmodules, no .git/modules entry and no
.git inside the directory -- so git tracks only a stale submodule SHA and
ignores the files entirely. The fix below therefore CANNOT be committed
normally; it lives on disk only and is lost by any checkout/clean/re-clone.
This patch is the durable copy. Re-apply with:

    git apply patches/0001-gen3_lite_2f-unique-gripper-hardware-name.patch

WHY IT MATTERS: <ros2_control name="GripperHardwareInterface"> was hardcoded
while every joint below it already used ${prefix}. With two or more Gen3 Lite
grippers loaded together -- i.e. always in `launch_workcell.sh full` --
ros2_control_node aborts at startup with
  std::runtime_error: Hardware name GripperHardwareInterface is duplicated
and nothing spawns: no controllers, no /joint_states, a disconnected TF tree,
and move_group complaining about missing frames. Deterministic, not flaky.

--- a/ros2_ws/src/ros2_kortex/kortex_description/grippers/gen3_lite_2f/urdf/gen3_lite_2f.ros2_control.xacro
+++ b/ros2_ws/src/ros2_kortex/kortex_description/grippers/gen3_lite_2f/urdf/gen3_lite_2f.ros2_control.xacro
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
         gripper_max_velocity:=100.0
         gripper_max_force:=100.0">
 
-        <ros2_control name="GripperHardwareInterface" type="system">
+        <ros2_control name="${prefix}GripperHardwareInterface" type="system">
             <hardware>
                 <xacro:if value="${sim_isaac}">
                     <plugin>topic_based_ros2_control/TopicBasedSystem</plugin>
